================================================================================
## Raise remaining Dependabot floors (authlib, dnspython, msgpack, nltk)
================================================================================

Context: After the 0.10.0 lock refresh, pip-audit / Dependabot still
listed authlib 1.7.2, dnspython 2.8.0, msgpack 1.2.1, and nltk 3.10.3.
Patched releases are now available. dnspython 2.9.0 requires Python
>=3.11, so the MCP server runtime floor matches the app. oauthlib 4.0.0
remains blocked by databricks-sql-connector.

Changes:

1. pyproject.toml
   Raise constraint floors for authlib>=1.9.1, dnspython>=2.9.0,
   msgpack>=1.2.3, and nltk>=3.10.4.
2. src/mcp-server/pyproject.toml
   Same Authlib/dnspython floors; require Python >=3.11.
3. uv.lock
   Resolve the new floors via the Databricks PyPI proxy, then rewrite
   URLs to files.pythonhosted.org / pypi.org/simple.
4. src/mcp-server/uv.lock
   Same regeneration for the standalone MCP graph.
5. docs/development.md
   Document the current security floors.

Modified files:
- pyproject.toml
- src/mcp-server/pyproject.toml
- uv.lock
- src/mcp-server/uv.lock
- docs/development.md
- changelogs/v0.10.0/benoitcayladbx_2026-10-30.log

Tests: uv run --frozen pytest -q -m "not scenario" -k "not test_readiness_route_returns_checks" → 9603 passed, 338 skipped, 9 deselected, 39 warnings in 39.54s
(The readiness route hung in this environment on a live dependency probe; it is unrelated to the lock rewrite and was excluded for this run.)

Still open (blocked upstream):
- oauthlib 4.0.0 — databricks-sql-connector pins oauthlib<4
- nltk GHSA-8mgp-746c-j5xp — no patched release yet

